{%- comment -%}
  Single source of truth for the sitewide Pharmacy entity's JSON-LD @id.
  Every schema node that describes Longeva as provider/publisher/about
  should reference this exact string via a bare { "@id": "..." } pointer
  rather than re-declaring the organization inline -- Google only merges
  JSON-LD nodes that share an identical @id string.

  Mirrors the canonical_origin computation in
  snippets/longeva-schema-pharmacy.liquid (the file that owns the full
  Pharmacy node this @id points at) so both always agree byte-for-byte.

  Usage (produces the bare "https://.../#pharmacy" string, no quotes):
    {% capture longeva_pharmacy_id %}{% render 'longeva-pharmacy-id' %}{% endcapture %}
    "@id": {{ longeva_pharmacy_id | json }}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign canonical_origin = shop.url | replace: 'http://', 'https://'
  unless canonical_origin contains 'https://'
    assign canonical_origin = canonical_origin | prepend: 'https:'
  endunless
-%}{{ canonical_origin }}/#pharmacy